hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18926","Abu Zakariyya Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us from his book, Ibn Lahiah informed us, and Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Amr, from Abu Thawr, and Ishaq al-Fahmi said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one day, when a garment of Maafir garments was brought. Abu Sufyan said: May Allah curse this garment and curse whoever makes for it. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not curse them, for they are from me and I am from them. Ishaq said: And may Allah curse whoever makes it."
